#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082924 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/id #uuid "e930a29a-6adf-5aaa-9b44-86dd8d570ae7" :question/math-academy-id "e-5354" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola\n$4 y^2 - 10 x^2 - 8 y - 40 x = 76$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4y^{2} - 10x^{2} - 8y - 40x &= 76 \\\\\n4y^{2} - 8y - 10x^{2} - 40x &= 76 \\\\\n4[y^{2} - 2y] - 10[x^{2} + 4x] &= 76 \\\\\n4[(y - 1)^{2} - 1] - 10[(x + 2)^{2} - 4] &= 76 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 4 - 10(x + 2)^{2} + 40 &= 76 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 10(x + 2)^{2} &= 76 - 40 + 4 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 10(x + 2)^{2} &= 40 \\\\\n((y - 1)^{2})/(10) - ((x + 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082991 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "0caa1041-a564-5428-9838-20cea32fdf17" :question/math-academy-id "e-6775" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2$.\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082992 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "8e31f5b5-ff87-5c45-b143-66dfdcb4ab8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6776" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3$.\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082993 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/id #uuid "af591507-e248-53d2-a391-e053cdc3fdea" :question/math-academy-id "e-6777" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola\n$x^2 - 4 y^2- 2 x + 16 y = 31$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 4y^{2} - 2x + 16y &= 31 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2x - 4y^{2} + 16y &= 31 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2x - 4[y^{2} - 4y] &= 31 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 - 4[(y - 2)^{2} - 4] &= 31 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 - 4(y - 2)^{2} + 16 &= 31 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 4(y - 2)^{2} &= 31 + 1 - 16 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 4(y - 2)^{2} &= 16 \\\\\n((x - 1)^{2})/(16) - ((y - 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(1,2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9060fa3-2fe0-57a2-95c1-50128575180a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263979} {:answer/id #uuid "7b632a05-16eb-5468-962a-55d83edd788c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263980} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf19b65-8c59-5ef3-b104-9ef16cdfbf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263981} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed0628e-5cbd-556f-b4c1-aa8f81743d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263982} {:answer/id #uuid "07d77eb6-3fad-5839-93b1-2c0e93a78163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9060fa3-2fe0-57a2-95c1-50128575180a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263979} :answer-field/id #uuid "3abf1bc2-758a-57fb-a501-411d6468b38c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70a4a2a9-00d7-57b7-8107-169920caa030" :question/math-academy-id "q-10419" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-16y-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-4y]-[{x}^{2}-4x] & =0 \\\\ 4[(y-2)^{2}-4]-[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-16-(x-2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =16-4 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abcfb624-f2a3-5d93-85c8-81747f7f5169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263986} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6bd005-39cb-5b95-8ed0-482ecffda449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263987} {:answer/id #uuid "8f50a3e4-875c-5112-bbd3-4af4b3b40f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263988} {:answer/id #uuid "03792036-0cf0-5d15-ab62-73a460fddbaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263989} {:answer/id #uuid "4648ecb8-4b69-5698-b0d5-a39dcb693fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4648ecb8-4b69-5698-b0d5-a39dcb693fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263990} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a525c2-17a1-5b6c-a397-8097118fff3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263985}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3668991-b7c7-5625-859d-527dc7e0482e" :question/math-academy-id "q-116082" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=-2$ and $k=4.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-2,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252aadde-fc49-510b-964d-6560603f4775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263993} {:answer/id #uuid "70aa6f67-40af-51b1-9cb3-624caa0fafae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263994} {:answer/id #uuid "00f1f4b8-8586-526f-80f5-af557a492ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263995} {:answer/id #uuid "952a4bd3-1d1f-5f7d-833c-cb0ed44de70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263996} {:answer/id #uuid "d30fcd45-2e64-5a29-89cc-0b65a3608754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70aa6f67-40af-51b1-9cb3-624caa0fafae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263994} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fb2c990-5b6d-5270-8354-fd909d63fc6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263992}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42c8badc-6c12-5e05-bb9d-6992afcc765d" :question/math-academy-id "q-116093" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{3}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-2$ and $k=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-2,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83a51fe9-b834-566b-9af3-5ce45eb97564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264000} {:answer/id #uuid "27c89026-7035-5d1b-a5aa-827bf8651707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16,36)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264001} {:answer/id #uuid "ea490062-99f2-5499-862a-51c46ddbecad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264002} {:answer/id #uuid "b3322d7e-8e93-5eaa-b517-065283180db4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264003} {:answer/id #uuid "9573dadd-fb0f-56b7-beb5-53091fb3e08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(36,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83a51fe9-b834-566b-9af3-5ce45eb97564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264000} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8056cb1-cc40-5c9a-86eb-42fa9219e28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263999}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de1381dc-294a-5282-98b1-fd2c2af9c202" :question/math-academy-id "q-116103" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{36}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-6))^{2}}{{6}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-6$ and $k=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-6,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9054894d-5f1a-5e91-9cff-3dadd34846ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264007} {:answer/id #uuid "533a5df7-b90d-5ab8-96fd-c3ca91be082b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264008} {:answer/id #uuid "05b72c06-5622-5552-90a7-a22c449df3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264009} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce28573-42fb-5f9b-a18c-f1f1d050efac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264010} {:answer/id #uuid "e83f19d2-1663-5270-b92e-93c9233d9e07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533a5df7-b90d-5ab8-96fd-c3ca91be082b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264008} :answer-field/id #uuid "356800a5-d904-5bd8-bf87-24af72734ba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3313b3b6-8b62-544d-8c3b-37c934a212ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-116123" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-10x+4y=31?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-10x+4y & =31 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+4y-{x}^{2}-10x & =31 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}+2y]-[{x}^{2}+10x] & =31 \\\\ 2[(y+1)^{2}-1]-[(x+5)^{2}-25] & =31 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-2-(x+5)^{2}+25 & =31 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-(x+5)^{2} & =31+2-25 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-(x+5)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-5))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-5,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac674c1c-f268-5436-8570-885d27bfa4ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080181} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1fdaea-fda0-5ce2-989e-5bbc86dbd375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080182} {:answer/id #uuid "3d67e170-c2c2-5fec-836d-bfcc4591e06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080183} {:answer/id #uuid "4f156fef-1336-5ed2-926d-4b2fc28fc5ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080184} {:answer/id #uuid "58d713c5-687a-52d6-8b97-0948d906e9a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad1fdaea-fda0-5ce2-989e-5bbc86dbd375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080182} :answer-field/id #uuid "3147a070-f252-5eab-abfe-a892dc36e0f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080180}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "025d6071-d0ec-5817-8d91-2087900261c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-16381" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola\n\n$6x^{2} - 5y^{2} + 72x + 70y = 59$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+72x+70y & =59 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+72x-5{y}^{2}+70y & =59 \\\\ 6[{x}^{2}+12x]-5[{y}^{2}-14y] & =59 \\\\ 6((x+6)^{2}-36)-5[(y-7)^{2}-49] & =59 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-216-5(y-7)^{2}+245 & =59 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-5(y-7)^{2} & =59+216-245 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-5(y-7)^{2} & =30 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-6,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81587eb5-1d6c-5f10-b88b-cc7ce81b91b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080187} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cb296a-75f9-5358-a33d-2d16559f3643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080188} {:answer/id #uuid "becbb8b2-bb50-5dcb-ab88-ff6b6afa048f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080189} {:answer/id #uuid "3af56a16-e77f-5f7b-92e6-8fe7e0dfc3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080190} {:answer/id #uuid "5c86004c-5604-516c-a114-409d8ed2ad1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af56a16-e77f-5f7b-92e6-8fe7e0dfc3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080190} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc496262-fe94-5383-a6ad-a471fe428a32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080186}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f42c289-2d52-53d8-afcb-0be869645e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-16382" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola\n\n$x^{2} - 5y^{2} + 2x + 10y = 9$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+2x+10y & =9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-5{y}^{2}+10y & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5[{y}^{2}-2y] & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5(y-1)^{2}+5 & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-5(y-1)^{2} & =9+1-5 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-5(y-1)^{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{5}-(y-1)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-1,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c39c2cc-56f3-5642-945c-087f873dbbaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} {:answer/id #uuid "c70d9036-7ad0-53ec-9ae2-f33ad6fe6619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c39c2cc-56f3-5642-945c-087f873dbbaf" :answer/type {